# Binary payloads. `core.autocrlf` is true in this repo, and without an explicit
# marking git decides text-vs-binary by sniffing the first 8000 bytes for a NUL. Every
# file below is framed with a JSON or text header ahead of its compressed payload, so
# that heuristic can flip to "text" as the header grows and then rewrite LF -> CRLF
# through the payload on checkout. `binary` is -diff -merge -text.

*.world         binary
*.world-delta   binary
*.fpak          binary
*.glb           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.png           binary
